                    'Whisky glasses, decanters, champagne flutes and wine glasses with names, a wedding date or a bar’s logo.',
                    'Glass coasters, magnets, keyrings and Christmas ornaments for larger batches.',
                ] ],
                [ 'p', 'The same machine can also personalise ceramic mugs, acrylic signs or plastic gadgets. Price each product based on the cost of the blank and the machine time.' ],
                [ 'h2', 'Wine glasses, tumblers and bottles: engraving with a rotary' ],
                [ 'p', 'On a flat bed you can only engrave a narrow strip of a cylinder, because the rest of the surface falls out of focus. Round glass needs a rotary attachment: it turns the item during the job, so the area being engraved always stays in focus and a design can wrap around the whole piece.' ],
                [ 'p', 'According to xTool’s data, two rotaries work with the F2 Ultra UV. The RA2 Pro has four modes: roller, chuck, sphere and ring. The RA3 (version 1) adds an enlarged 130 mm chuck for larger items and batch processing on rollers and in the jaws. If you are considering the Business Duo, check compatibility: the RA3 supports both the F2 Ultra UV and the F2 Ultra, while the RA2 Pro’s compatibility list includes the F2 Ultra UV but not the F2 Ultra.' ],
                [ 'products', '8309744009429,9089336017109' ],
                [ 'h2', 'When does the Business Duo make sense?' ],
