                [ 'products', '9341134569685,8536169742549' ],
                [ 'h2', 'Practical tips: material, tests and cleanliness' ],
                [ 'ul', [
                    'Choose K9 crystal, an optical glass, for 3D engraving. According to xTool, it is purer than ordinary soda-lime glass, so the inner engraving comes out clean.',
                    'Clean the surface before engraving. xTool recommends alcohol for crystal blocks and a soft, dry cloth for wine glasses, because dust and fingerprints show in the finished piece. Handle crystal with gloves.',
                    'Crystal balls are engraved fully submerged in inner engraving oil. The curved surface acts like a lens and bends the beam, and the oil reduces that effect. xTool recommends an oil level 2 mm above the ball; the oil can be reused until it turns cloudy, and the ball should only be rinsed with water once engraving is finished.',
                    'Test on a piece from the same batch. Glass from different suppliers differs in composition and thickness. xTool Selected materials come with a QR code holding ready-made settings: place the code card in the machine and refresh the camera view.',
